{"id":"shemaiah","name":"Shemaiah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:shemaiah"],"types":[],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":["1. A prophet in the time of Rehoboam"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Shemaiah","text":"Whom Jehovah heard. (1.) A prophet in the reign of Rehoboam (1 Kings 12:22-24). (2.) Neh. 3:29. (3.) A Simeonite (1 Chr. 4:37). (4.) A priest (Neh. 12:42). (5.) A Levite (1 Chr. 9:16). (6.) 1 Chr. 9:14; Neh. 11:15. (7.) A Levite in the time of David, who with 200 of his brethren took part in the bringing up of the ark from Obed-edom to Hebron (1 Chr. 15:8). (8.) A Levite (1 Chr. 24:6). (9.) The eldest son of Obed-edom (1 Chr. 26:4-8). (10.) A Levite (2 Chr. 29:14). (11.) A false prophet who hindered the rebuilding of Jerusalem (Neh. 6:10). (12.) A prince of Judah who assisted at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem (Neh. 12:34-36). (13.) A false prophet who opposed Jeremiah (Jer. 29:24-32). (14.) One of the Levites whom Jehoshaphat appointed to teach the law (2 Chr. 17:8). (15.) A Levite appointed to “distribute the oblations of the Lord” (2 Chr. 31:15). (16.) A Levite (2 Chr. 35:9). …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8098","lemma":"שְׁמַעְיָה","xlit":"Shᵉmaʻyâh","gloss":"Shemajah, the name of twenty-five Israelites","kjv":"Shemaiah","count":39,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":26,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H3548","lemma":"כֹּהֵן","xlit":"kôhên","gloss":"one officiating, a priest","kjv":"chief ruler, own, priest, prince","count":9,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H251","lemma":"אָח","xlit":"ʼâch","gloss":"a brother )","kjv":"another, brother; kindred, like, other","count":8,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H1004","lemma":"בַּיִת","xlit":"bayith","gloss":"a house","kjv":"court, daughter, door, dungeon","count":11,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H1697","lemma":"דָּבָר","xlit":"dâbâr","gloss":"a word","kjv":"act